# Project-specific — extractor outputs are reproducible and large; only the
# per-extractor README (setup notes + version pinning) is tracked. Negation
# patterns require the parent dirs to NOT be excluded with trailing-slash,
# so we ignore everything inside via `**` then re-include the dir tree.
samples/extractor-output/**
!samples/extractor-output/
!samples/extractor-output/*/
!samples/extractor-output/*/README.md
samples/raw-pdfs/**
!samples/raw-pdfs/
# samples/raw-docx/ is NOT ignored — see CLAUDE.md "Sample primary sources".
# DOCX files are user-uploaded primary sources (e.g., legislative bills) that
# can't be auto-fetched from a public URL the way PDFs can. Committing them
# keeps them on disk across worktrees and fresh clones.
#
# Same logic for the AGAO Annual Financial Report — its source URL on
# gao.az.gov is gated behind a Cloudflare bot challenge that returns 403 to
# every programmatic client (curl/httpx/PowerShell) even with full browser
# headers. Functionally a user-uploaded primary source. Commit it so future
# worktrees / fresh clones don't need to manually re-download via a browser.
# See docs/superpowers/investigations/2026-05-07-publisher-portals.md.
!samples/raw-pdfs/agao-afr-fy25.pdf

# Phase 1a runtime data — large, reproducible. The smaller curated
# artifacts (data/discovery-cache.yaml, data/fund-catalog.yaml,
# data/system-prompt-context.md, data/ingest-plan.yaml) ARE tracked.
data/cached-pdfs/
data/extractor-output/
# data/chunks/ chunk JSONs ARE committed — decision per
# PROMPT-volume-ingest.md "Commit policy": persist across machines so
# volume ingest doesn't have to re-run on every clone (1-2hr GPU run +
# ~28MB total compressed — well under any practical Git size limit).
# extractor-output/ and cached-pdfs/ stay gitignored above; those are
# the bulky reproducible inputs.
# Audit JSON outputs are reproducible — gitignore.
data/audit/

# mineru-api daemon writes per-request <task-id>/ subdirs under output/
# in whatever CWD it's launched from. Reproducible from the source PDFs +
# the dispatcher's own per-doc extractor-output/<doc_id>/manifest.json
# sidecar; we don't need a second copy in the repo. Leaving these tracked
# would add ~390MB of UUID-named noise per volume-ingest run.
output/

*.tmp
.tmp-*/

# Postgres / database
*.db
*.sqlite
postgres-data/
# Phase 1b local-dev Postgres data volume (Docker compose bind mount)
db/data/

# Test artifacts
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Companion app builds
companion-dist/
companion-out/
